@prefix backlog: <http://example.org/backlog#> .
@prefix ex:      <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1011simp-lineage#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<http://example.org/sen0414-ch1011simp-lineage> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Urgent narrow lineage: SEN0414 chapters 10 and 11, one code, one environment"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.27.0" ; owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1011simp-lineage/1.27.0> ; dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch1011simp_lineage" ;
    rdfs:comment """1.27.0 (2026-11-24): Scope change only (one stage per version). The Owner asked at 11:14 Istanbul what the page's concept panels are and said that they must be book compliant unless there is another reason against it. Discipline files re-read from GitHub at this step: OE 2.41.0 and Lineage 163.0.7, unchanged."""@en .

ex:CR11_ConceptPanels a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "Make the concept panels and the chapter examples pane of the page book compliant"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope11 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Owner's instruction of 2026-11-24 11:14 Istanbul (content, not a verbatim quotation): the page concept panels must be book compliant if there are no other reasons against that." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .

ex:IA11_ConceptPanels a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What the concept panels hold today, measured before anything is planned"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR11_ConceptPanels ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage11 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "MEASURED FACTS (2026-11-24, read-only, from page data 9.21.0 of chapter 10 and 9.22.0 of chapter 11): a concept panel is the page card of one concept of the chapter; it holds the explanation, the book's own line for the concept (chapter 10: 39 of 59 panels; chapter 11: 44 of 64) and a Try it run (36 and 42). The Try it runs are not book code: 32 of the 36 in chapter 10 and all 42 in chapter 11 are one-line expressions written for the page with import and temporary-folder tricks, stored in the chapter's domain A-box (hasIOExample) and run by page data 2.29.0. The Lab pane Chapter examples (18 in chapter 10, 19 in chapter 11) still reads the old deck transcript, not the book code. Both are the first objection of 2026-11-20 (code that is not the book's) left standing on the page. REASONS AGAINST that hold: a book line that is only a fragment (an ellipsis, a bare method call, a security warning) cannot run alone, so it runs inside the book program of the chapter source that holds it, or carries a named reason, as the source already does. IMPACT: the A-box of each chapter gets a new version whose Try it inputs are the book's lines with the hidden set-up of the source; the Chapter examples pane is made from the manifest; both pages are rebuilt and tested again. No slide changes." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Cost named: a new A-box version and a new page version for each of the two chapters, one more story each, and a new page test run each (about 16 minutes). The deck and the source stay unchanged unless a book line needs a program that the source does not hold." .

ex:Area11_Concepts a backlog:ScopeArea ; rdfs:label "Concept panels and chapter examples of the page follow the book"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage11 .
ex:Del11_Concepts_10 a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "Chapter 10 page whose concept panels and chapter examples run the book's code"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage11 ; backlog:deliverableForArea ex:Area11_Concepts .
ex:Del11_Concepts_11 a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "Chapter 11 page whose concept panels and chapter examples run the book's code"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage11 ; backlog:deliverableForArea ex:Area11_Concepts .

ex:SC11_ConceptPanels a backlog:ScopeChange ;
    rdfs:label "Scope grown by book-compliant concept panels for chapters 10 and 11"@en ;
    backlog:fulfillsRequest ex:CR11_ConceptPanels ; backlog:changesScope ex:Scope11 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner ;
    backlog:admitsItem ex:Area11_Concepts, ex:Del11_Concepts_10, ex:Del11_Concepts_11 ;
    backlog:hasScopeChangeRationale "Owner's instruction of 2026-11-24 11:14 Istanbul. The boundary moves outward by one area and two deliverables; the exclusion of other chapters stays. Cost named: two more rebuilds and page tests in this urgent lineage; the urgency case is resolved only after these are done." .
ex:Scope11 backlog:coversArea ex:Area11_Concepts ; backlog:hasScopeDeliverable ex:Del11_Concepts_10, ex:Del11_Concepts_11 .
